class PriorityQueue(): 

    def __init__(self): 
        self.elements = [] 

    def is_empty(self): 
        return len(self.elements) == 0 

    def enqueue(self, item, priority): 
        self.elements.append((item, priority)) 

    def dequeue(self): 
        max_priority_index = 0
        for index, element in enumerate(self.elements): 
            if element[1] > self.elements[max_priority_index][1]: 
                max_priority_index = index 
        element = self.elements[max_priority_index] 
        del self.elements[max_priority_index] 
        return element
```

Given the following array of dictionaries, write a function in Python to find and return the longest common prefix in the keys of dictionaries.

